       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. The maximum FDA-labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day, and that is for immediate-release metformin. A dose three times that raises the risk of severe lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day total and the usual maximum.\n- A lower dose, such as 500 mg PO twice daily or 500 mg PO three times daily. Many clinicians start low and titrate up.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 2550 mg per dose was intentional, please confirm that. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy or your attending first."
